    "turn_idx": 74,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and it's a trend that we've seen earlier as well. I remember Ted Cruz last year was hounded at a restaurant with his wife, and they were going to leave, but then the restaurant got rid of the protesters. Sarah Huckabee Sanders was actually asked to leave a restaurant in Virginia by the people who ran the restaurant because of her political activity. And we've seen other football players say that they're not going to the White House with their team. uh... during to celebrate with the president so i think it is part of an ongoing thing i mean look so i think part of it is the you know the political views themselves have become very sharply polarized but i think a lot of it just has to do with the tone of the discourse you know uh... i mean certain as certain things that uh... you know president obama even even uh... advocated A few years ago, I saw on Twitter, like in 2014, in an interview with ABC, he was talking about stopping migrants at the border and sending them back, saying that kids, we need to send a message not to have kids sent to the border. Well, that's the same exact policy that Trump and border security are affecting. But for some reason, when Trump does it, it's just beyond the pale. And I think that has to do with the issue of a bad faith, a lack of trust, and general tone, which just inflames everything.",
